BT 1 0 0 1 0 97 Tm -0.005566 Tw 15.5 TL 1 1 1 rg /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Our agenda, the ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (Principles of Self-Defence under Article 51 of the UN Charter) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (, is one of the oldest and most) Tj T* 0 Tw (contested questions in the law of the Charter. Few provisions are cited as often, and few are read so) Tj T* (differently by different States. We do not expect you to settle it. We expect you to ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (argue it) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 15.5 TL (: from the text,) Tj T* (from the case law of the International Court of Justice, from State practice, and from your own delegation's) Tj T* -0.060156 Tw (record. A delegate who only repeats that self-defence is an inherent right, or that force is prohibited, will not) Tj T* 0 Tw (hold the floor for long. A delegate who can explain which conditions are met or unmet, on what evidence,) Tj T* (and at what cost to the system as a whole will drive the debate.) Tj T* ET
