BT 1 0 0 1 0 117.2 Tm 14.3 TL 1 1 1 rg /F3+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (This committee runs as a General Assembly and not as a crisis committee. However, the Executive Board) Tj T* (may introduce ) Tj /F4+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (crisis updates) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL ( \(for example, a notification to the Security Council invoking Article 51, or a) Tj T* (sudden cross-border incident\) to test the committee's ability to apply the principles under debate. A crisis) Tj T* (update is an update that describes developments and clearly describes the current situation in committee.) Tj T* /F6+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (Example of a crisis update: At 0600 hours, satellite imagery released by an independent monitor shows the) Tj  T* /F6+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (mobilisation of armed forces along a disputed frontier. At 0930 hours, one State notifies the Security Council) Tj  T* /F6+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (that it is taking measures in self-defence under Article 51, and a second State describes those measures as an) Tj  T* /F6+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL (act of aggression.) Tj /F3+0 11.5 Tf 14.3 TL ( After a crisis update, the floor for directives will be open, and delegates may play with the) Tj T* (update and conduct their own national operations through directives, communiques and press releases.) Tj T* ET
